# Phase-6 different-config in-process probe — config A, the CONTAMINANT.
# Run FIRST inside the shared interpreter, purely to populate whatever
# module-level state trinity leaks, then discarded. Deliberately unlike config B:
# 10x the cloud mass, 1/3 the SFE and 1/10 the core density, so the SPS f_mass
# scaling and the density/temperature region queried in the cooling cube both
# differ from B's.
# stop_t is tiny because only the caches A leaves behind matter, not A's physics.
mCloud    1e6
sfe    0.1
nCore    1e4
stop_t    0.01
